   "item_id": "rp-04",
   "split": "test",
   "category": "method",
   "answerable": true,
   "status": "answered",
   "answer": "According to [1], several machine learning classifiers are used to calculate accuracy and performance based on the category and attributes of the resume.\n\n[2] also mentions that the KNN (K-Nearest Neighbors) classifier is used in the context of resume screening, but it does not specify the exact classifiers used.\n\n[3] mentions that the task is to rank the resumes based on the content of the resume match with the job description file, but it does not specify the exact classifiers used.\n\nThe only specific classifiers mentioned in the sources are SVM (Support Vector Machine) and Random Forest, but only in [5] as part of the introduction, not as part of the system's classification process.\n\nTherefore, I could not find the answer to this question in the provided documents, as the sources do not explicitly mention the specific classifiers used for resume classification.",
