   "item_id": "rp-05",
   "split": "dev",
   "category": "method",
   "answerable": true,
   "status": "answered",
   "answer": "According to the provided sources, resumes are compared with the job description using the Vector Space Model [Arguello and Jaime, 2013][1] and similarity measures like cosine similarity [Huang and Anna, 2008][2]. The cosine similarity is used to measure the best fitting resume for the given job description.\n\nAdditionally, the K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) method is used, which works by finding the K resumes that are most similar to a given job posting based on their features [5]. The job ad is then categorized by KNN using the class that has the most members among its K nearest neighbors.\n\nIt is not explicitly stated how the ranking is done, but it is mentioned that the system takes a bulk of resumes and job description and ranks them based on the job constraint provided [3].",
   "status_correct": true,
   "hallucinated": false,
